<title>BELGIUM: EU vets Cereol stake in Olmuhle.</title>
<headline>EU vets Cereol stake in Olmuhle.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it was starting a routine probe into a proposal by Cereol Holding BV, which belongs to Eridania Beghin-Say, to buy a 50-percent stake in oilseed processor Olmuhle GmbH from Austrian holding OSAT.</p>
<p>It said the deal was submitted to it for clearance on February 27 under the European Union's merger rules which ban creation or strengthening of dominant positions. It has a month from that date to approve it or start a full probe.</p>
<p>OSAT currently controls 100 percent of Olmuhle.</p>
<p>Cereol also processes oilseeds and produces and markets seed oil, meal and biofuel. -- Brussels newsroom 322 2876841</p>
